{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial`.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "I found one gap: no test checks that an unresolvable mandatory input is reported before inference. Everything else is implemented, marked, and tested.\n\n**Obligations and the code that carries them out**\n- **Combine the applicable contributions.**\n  - `AssessmentSources::prepare` (`src/authoring/inputs.rs`) combines the subject's own declaration, its `{cite}`d requirements, and built-ins.\n  - It adds the owning outline nodes of `{impl}`/`{test}` references and of `:impl:`/`:test:` anchors.\n  - It adds the terminology via `definition_inputs`.\n  - `prepare_citation` does the same for citation reviews.\n  - `AuthoringSubject::sources` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`) selects between the two.\n  - Tests: `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors`, `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs`, `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs`, `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes`, and `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once`.\n- **Include every applicable contribution.** The same code and tests cover this.\n- **Deduplicate identical selections.** `insert_selector` and the `contains` checks around `definition_inputs` do this. The citation-review test asserts that each declaration, term, and built-in appears once.\n- **Supply the complete set in the initial model request.**\n  - `initial_prompt` renders `mandatory_inputs()` into the prompt, and `converse` records them as pending.\n  - `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free`, `initial_prompt_substitutes_subject_and_mandatory_inputs_into_the_template`, and `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` check the prompt content.\n- **Omit generated `evidence/` output by default, including symlink aliases.**\n  - `omit_generated_evidence`, `generated_evidence_path`, and `generated_evidence_selector` do this.\n  - `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` and `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` cover it.\n- **An explicit workspace allow permits the selection.** `omit_generated_evidence` returns false when the policy allows the path. The anchors test covers this.\n- **An explicit disallow aborts under `read_denial`.** `SourceAccess::file` and `source_input` return `PermissionDenied`. The anchors test and `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation` cover it, and `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` covers the outside-the-project case.\n- **Report unresolvable mandatory inputs.** `prepare` and `prepare_citation` return errors. `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` and `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation` cover this, and the citation test covers a disallowed term.\n- **A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this one.** This binds requirement texts, not code. The references listing shows the contributing chapters citing it.\n\n**Gap**\n- **Report unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference.**\n  - The ordering lives in `configured_record` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`): `subject.sources(root)?` runs before `RigProvider::connect` and `assess_subject`.\n  - Every test I found calls `AssessmentSources::prepare` or `prepare_citation` directly and asserts the error.\n  - None runs the CLI or `configured_record` with an unresolvable mandatory input and asserts that no model request is made and no evidence is written.\n  - The denial tests that do check request counts, `explicit_untracked_reads_abort_without_another_request_or_evidence_write` and the batch denial tests, deny a read the model makes mid-conversation, not a mandatory input.\n  - The batch test `unreadable_reference_sources_fail_the_batch_before_inference` covers discovery failures, not mandatory-input preparation.\n  - This obligation is stated in the text and the sequencing code has a failure branch, so it needs its own test. No `{fixme}` acknowledges the gap.",
  "references": "b9eea9d9d6ca6312e293dc19222ceca1fa0417d7b4d228f676a47c13dfa284f7",
